    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d586">

                <pb facs="0690" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg622"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/3576¾</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 11, 1917</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Enclosed are tentative
                    regulations drawn up for the government of the Armed Guard to be placed on
                    merchant ships. Will you be good enough to suggest any changes, additions or
                    omissions that you think will be wise? We wish to send <pb facs="0691" n="623"
                        xml:id="pg623"/> these instructions out on Monday. I will be glad to call to
                    go over this matter if you desire.</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Josephus Daniels</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Please return enclosed with your suggestions.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d586-a1.xml" xpointer="d586-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
